1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:03,600
Is NEAR Intents real settlement?

2
00:00:03,600 --> 00:00:06,800
And does it create value for NEAR?

3
00:00:07,200 --> 00:00:11,200
Up front: real infrastructure, thin value for the token.

4
00:00:11,200 --> 00:00:14,800
Every figure carries its date range.

5
00:00:15,200 --> 00:00:23,000
$1.30B net swap volume, 2026-09-29 → 2026-10-28, read straight from intents.near event logs.

6
00:00:23,000 --> 00:00:31,800
About 35% of reported volume is confidential and invisible on-chain. Public events only, read from the logs.

7
00:00:32,200 --> 00:00:40,000
99.96% of 4.2M implicit accounts are used on one day only. In October, just 0.22% were active twice or more.

8
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:48,800
So account counts can't prove adoption. Every chart ships the SQL behind it.

9
00:00:49,400 --> 00:00:55,000
Captured revenue: $26.2M a year, 0.43% of NEAR's market cap.

10
00:00:55,000 --> 00:01:03,800
Even at 10x today's volume it would be 4.28% of market cap.

11
00:01:04,200 --> 00:01:09,800
One command re-runs the whole thesis: no accounts, no keys.

12
00:01:09,800 --> 00:01:15,800
The numbers don't move. (Terminal sped up 2.1x.)

13
00:01:16,500 --> 00:01:23,500
Ask the chain. Show the work.
